mainmenu "AD9081 JESD204B bring-up sample"

config AD9081_FAULT_INJECTION
	bool "Run JESD204 fault-injection tests after bring-up"
	help
	  Exercise the failure and recovery paths that a successful bring-up
	  never reaches: the FSM's failure accounting, the RX lane-desync
	  watchdog, link teardown followed by a second bring-up, and a GT
	  transceiver that cannot lock its PLL.

	  Enabling this compiles test-only hooks into axi_jesd204.c and
	  axi_adxcvr.c that let the tests force a lane-status value and
	  mis-program the RX GT clock mux. With it disabled (the default) none
	  of that code is built.

	  The tests deliberately break a working link and then rebuild it, so
	  do not leave this on in a normal build.

config AD9081_ADXCVR_INIT_PRIORITY
	int "AXI-ADXCVR (GT transceiver) init priority"
	default 65
	help
	  Initialisation priority of the AXI-ADXCVR driver, within POST_KERNEL.

	  Must be above CONFIG_CLOCK_CONTROL_HMC7044_INIT_PRIORITY: the adxcvr
	  nodes take `clocks = <&hmc7044 12>`, and Zephyr's init-priority
	  validation rejects a device that initialises before a devicetree
	  dependency. There is a BUILD_ASSERT in axi_adxcvr.c for it.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
